   "title": "Faded colour recovery: single frame",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Faded colour recovery: single frame\n\nOne faded frame in, one colour frame out, with the frame's own brightness kept.\n\n1. **Source frame**: your faded frame (PNG). The test frame is `source.png` from *Counter Attack* (1976).\n2. **Colour chart**: `chart.png`, a softly blurred colour chart. Keep it; it guides the colour and gives the model nothing else to copy.\n3. **Edge map**: `control.png`, the Canny edges of the source. For your own frame, connect **Detect Edges** below instead (right-click the Edge map input of both *Encode* nodes' image3, or just drag the Canny output into *Scale edge map*).\n\nModel: the published model (fp8mixed). Lightning 4-step LoRA, cfg 0.9, seed 0, shift 3.1.\n\nOutputs: **model output** (1184 \u00d7 880, the raw proposal) and **composite** (the proposal's colour on the source's brightness, at source size). Review both against the source: altered faces, invented objects, colour across an edge, clipped highlights.\n\nResearch by Fabio Bedoya. Generated colour is an interpretation, not evidence of the original colour. fabiocolor.github.io/experimental-film-restoration-ml/colour-recovery/"
   ],
   "color": "#3b3b2e",
   "bgcolor": "#5a5a3a"
  },
