   "title": "Composite",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "**Composite.** The model returns a reduced picture (1184 \u00d7 880 for 4:3). Only its colour is used: the result is scaled back to the source size, its U and V (colour) are joined to the source's Y (brightness). Grain, detail and damage are the source's. Plain scaling and a shadow gate (right); the kit's `composite_still.py` is the reference, with the exact inverse of the Kontext crop and a smoothstep gate."
   ],
   "color": "#3b3b2e",
   "bgcolor": "#5a5a3a"
  },
